1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,760
Hey, welcome back.

2
00:00:00,960 --> 00:00:02,500
And in this video, we're gonna have a look

3
00:00:02,500 --> 00:00:04,280
at ChatGPT projects.

4
00:00:04,740 --> 00:00:07,460
You can think of ChatGPT projects a little bit like a folder.

5
00:00:07,880 --> 00:00:10,000
You can put specific information in there,

6
00:00:10,160 --> 00:00:12,240
files, custom instructions.

7
00:00:12,680 --> 00:00:15,340
Whenever you have a project or something specific,

8
00:00:15,380 --> 00:00:18,060
I'd recommend putting it inside of a ChatGPT project.

9
00:00:18,420 --> 00:00:20,500
That way you can keep everything nice and tidy.

10
00:00:20,780 --> 00:00:22,000
And when you're specifically wanting

11
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:23,140
to talk about that project,

12
00:00:23,300 --> 00:00:24,980
you'll then navigate into that project

13
00:00:24,980 --> 00:00:26,940
and go into it almost like a folder.

14
00:00:27,420 --> 00:00:29,020
Let's see how we can create projects.

15
00:00:29,020 --> 00:00:30,600
Go over to the left-hand side,

16
00:00:30,920 --> 00:00:32,860
and then you can see you've got projects

17
00:00:32,860 --> 00:00:34,400
above your chat history.

18
00:00:34,920 --> 00:00:36,440
I want you to click on New Project,

19
00:00:36,860 --> 00:00:38,620
and then I want you to give your project a name.

20
00:00:38,760 --> 00:00:40,460
I'm gonna call mine Travel Holidays,

21
00:00:41,440 --> 00:00:43,320
and then you're gonna click Create Project.

22
00:00:43,900 --> 00:00:45,900
It will take a little bit of time to create a project,

23
00:00:46,100 --> 00:00:47,220
so we'll just wait for that.

24
00:00:47,440 --> 00:00:49,400
After you've got a project that's being created,

25
00:00:49,560 --> 00:00:51,320
you can add files to this project.

26
00:00:51,460 --> 00:00:54,600
Now, these files are specifically attached to this project,

27
00:00:54,600 --> 00:00:56,840
so you can add custom instructions,

28
00:00:56,840 --> 00:00:59,000
so what kind of things are specific to this project.

29
00:00:59,240 --> 00:01:05,060
So I'll say, only give me advice about where to go,

30
00:01:05,760 --> 00:01:07,120
not what to eat.

31
00:01:07,760 --> 00:01:09,240
We can also drag in files,

32
00:01:09,760 --> 00:01:12,080
and you can see that this uses the default memory.

33
00:01:12,260 --> 00:01:14,560
So projects can access memories from outside chats

34
00:01:14,560 --> 00:01:15,480
and vice versa.

35
00:01:15,920 --> 00:01:18,140
So it will access your default memory.

36
00:01:18,740 --> 00:01:20,920
You can add files and instructions.

37
00:01:21,520 --> 00:01:22,680
And what's clever about this

38
00:01:22,680 --> 00:01:24,900
is that these instructions and these files

39
00:01:24,900 --> 00:01:27,080
are only specific to this project.

40
00:01:27,760 --> 00:01:29,900
So that means I could have a specific way

41
00:01:29,900 --> 00:01:32,420
of talking with chat GPT inside of a project.

42
00:01:32,720 --> 00:01:34,040
Let's say I've asked, for example,

43
00:01:34,180 --> 00:01:35,760
I want to go on holiday to Brazil,

44
00:01:35,920 --> 00:01:37,100
can you give me some recommendations?

45
00:01:37,800 --> 00:01:40,060
You'll see it's given us some information about this,

46
00:01:40,220 --> 00:01:41,660
specific places to go.

47
00:01:42,040 --> 00:01:44,340
That's great, but now if we look on the left-hand side,

48
00:01:44,480 --> 00:01:47,540
can you see our Travel Holidays folder or project

49
00:01:47,540 --> 00:01:49,700
has now got a recent chat history.

50
00:01:50,200 --> 00:01:51,600
Now, if I click on this again,

51
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:54,100
you'll see that we've got our one conversation here,

52
00:01:54,100 --> 00:01:56,140
so we can actually share this conversation.

53
00:01:56,680 --> 00:01:58,440
We can re-engage with this conversation.

54
00:01:59,020 --> 00:02:00,380
So it's a way for you to,

55
00:02:00,680 --> 00:02:03,060
rather than have a load of your conversations

56
00:02:03,060 --> 00:02:04,800
and you're endlessly scrolling,

57
00:02:05,140 --> 00:02:07,420
trying to find that conversation that you had,

58
00:02:07,800 --> 00:02:09,740
that's where you're starting to use projects, right?

59
00:02:09,820 --> 00:02:12,660
So when you've got 100 or 300 different types

60
00:02:12,660 --> 00:02:13,740
of chat GPT conversations,

61
00:02:14,120 --> 00:02:15,640
you just can't seem to find them.

62
00:02:15,880 --> 00:02:17,920
So that's a really, really good use case

63
00:02:17,920 --> 00:02:20,620
for using these projects inside of chat GPT.

64
00:02:21,260 --> 00:02:23,020
One other thing that I really like to do is,

65
00:02:23,020 --> 00:02:25,780
let's say I create a new conversation outside of the project.

66
00:02:26,040 --> 00:02:29,720
So I'm looking to learn about Spain and travel.

67
00:02:30,220 --> 00:02:32,220
One way that I like to do this is you'll see

68
00:02:32,220 --> 00:02:34,360
that over here in the sort of left-hand side,

69
00:02:34,700 --> 00:02:36,880
the conversations come up about Spain,

70
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:40,280
but I really wanted to have had that inside of my project.

71
00:02:40,320 --> 00:02:41,720
So you can just click on the triple dots

72
00:02:41,720 --> 00:02:44,740
and then you can move that to a specific project,

73
00:02:44,920 --> 00:02:45,660
so Travel Holidays.

74
00:02:46,060 --> 00:02:48,500
And now that Spain information is there

75
00:02:48,500 --> 00:02:49,740
with my Brazil information.

76
00:02:50,140 --> 00:02:51,980
So it's kind of one of these things where like,

77
00:02:51,980 --> 00:02:56,000
if you do forget to specifically talk inside of a project,

78
00:02:56,200 --> 00:02:57,880
then you can always move that chat session

79
00:02:57,880 --> 00:02:59,740
over into the project itself.

80
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:01,900
So I find these two ways of working

81
00:03:01,900 --> 00:03:03,920
are really, really good for tidying up.

82
00:03:04,360 --> 00:03:06,500
And then I don't have to manually search all the chats.

83
00:03:06,580 --> 00:03:08,320
I can just keep the relevant chats

84
00:03:08,320 --> 00:03:09,720
under a specific project.

85
00:03:10,060 --> 00:03:11,700
The other benefit that you get though from this

86
00:03:11,700 --> 00:03:14,360
is that as you talk more in a specific project,

87
00:03:14,760 --> 00:03:17,100
chat GPT is clever enough to pull in relevant types

88
00:03:17,100 --> 00:03:19,600
of chats within side that project itself.

89
00:03:19,660 --> 00:03:21,340
So it starts to remember things specifically

90
00:03:21,340 --> 00:03:23,560
from chat histories that have happened

91
00:03:23,560 --> 00:03:24,500
inside of that project.

92
00:03:24,960 --> 00:03:26,460
You can also add files.

93
00:03:26,700 --> 00:03:28,560
I don't find myself doing that much,

94
00:03:28,820 --> 00:03:31,260
but obviously if you're in data analysis

95
00:03:31,260 --> 00:03:34,920
or you're pulling in relevant CSVs or PDF files or images,

96
00:03:35,400 --> 00:03:36,660
then you can certainly include that

97
00:03:36,660 --> 00:03:37,960
at the project level as well.

98
00:03:38,380 --> 00:03:38,740
Okay, great.

99
00:03:39,080 --> 00:03:39,760
So that was projects.

100
00:03:40,220 --> 00:03:41,120
I'll see you in the next one.
